CloudBurrow patch 67 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1562).

MOD converted both arguments to float64, so an INT64 above 2^53 lost
its low bits: MOD(9223372036854775807, 3) was 2, not 1. Two INT64s are
taken by integer remainder, which has the sign of X, as BigQuery
documents.

